"The Eulerian transformation - Science Explorer Abstract (https://scixplorer.org/abs/2021arXiv210300890B/abstract)\nciteturn2search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.7 years ago; Crawled: last month; We give combinatorial, topological and Ehrhart theoretic interpretations of the operator $\\mathcal{A}$, and investigate questions of unimodality and real-rootedness. In particular, we disprove a conjecture by Brenti (1989) concerning the preservation of real zeros, and generalize and strengthen recent results of Haglund and Zhang (2019) on binomial Eulerian polynomials. ... Publication  | eprint arXiv:2103.00890\n\n## The Eulerian transformation\n\n### Authors\n\nBrändén, Petter;\n\nJochemko, Katharina\n\nEprint\n\nFull Text Sources\n\nOther Resources\n\n### Abstract\n\nEulerian polynomials are fundamental in combinatorics and algebra. In this paper we study the linear transformation $\\mathcal{A} : \\mathbb{R}[t] \\to \\mathbb{R}[t]$ defined by $\\mathcal{A}(t^n) = A_n(t)$, where $A_n(t)$ denotes the $n$-th Eulerian polynomial. We give combinatorial, topological and Ehrhart theoretic interpretations of the operator $\\mathcal{A}$, and investigate questions of unimodality and real-rootedness. In particular, we disprove a conjecture by Brenti (1989) concerning the preservation of real zeros, and generalize and strengthen recent results of Haglund and Zhang (2019) on binomial Eulerian polynomials.\n\n### Details\n\nPublication  | eprint arXiv:2103.00890\nPublication Date  | March 2021\nDOI  | 10.48550/arXiv.2103.00890\narXiv  | arXiv:2103.00890\nBibcode  | 2021arXiv210300890B\nCollection  | general\nKeyword  | Mathematics - Combinatorics\nE-Print Comment(s)  | 17 pages, 2 figures; v2: minor changes; accepted for publication in Trans. Amer. Math. Soc--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nReal-rootedness of the Eulerian transformation on the binomial basis cone | MathDB (https://mathdb.com/p/349953/real-rootedness-of-the-eulerian-transformation-on-the-binomi)\nciteturn2search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; This conjecture seeks a restricted real-rootedness-preservation property after Brenti's broader conjecture was disproved. ... Petter Brändén and Katharina Jochemko, “The Eulerian transformation”, arXiv:2103.00890 (2021).\n\n# Real-rootedness of the Eulerian transformation on the binomial basis cone\n\nAbout 5 years old · traced to 2021\n\nLet $n\\geq 0$n≥0, and let $f$f be a polynomial of the form\n\n$$f=\\sum_{k=0}^n a_k t^k(1+t)^{n-k},\\qquad a_k\\geq 0\\quad(0\\leq k\\leq n).$$f=k=0∑n​a k​t k(1+t)n−k,a k​≥0(0≤k≤n).\n\nLet $\\operatorname*{\\mathcal E}:\\mathbb{R}[t]\\to\\mathbb{R}[t]$E:R[t]→R[t] be the Eulerian transformation defined by $\\operatorname*{\\mathcal E}(t^m)=A_m(t)$E(t m)=A m​(t), where $A_m(t)$A m​(t) is the $m$m-th Eulerian polynomial. The paper's conjecture. The polynomial $\\operatorname*{\\mathcal E}(f)$E(f) is real-rooted.\n\nThis conjecture seeks a restricted real-rootedness-preservation property after Brenti's broader conjecture was disproved. The paper provides partial evidence, including alternatingly increasing and hence unimodal coefficients for the transformed polynomials, as well as real-rootedness results for important subfamilies; the full assertion remains open in the supplied text.\n\nReferences\n\n## Primary source\n\nPetter Brändén and Katharina Jochemko, “The Eulerian transformation”, arXiv:2103.00890 (2021).\n\ncombinatoricseulerian-polynomialsreal-rootedness\n\n## Progress summary\n\nRefresh Never refreshed\n\nNothing recorded yet. Refresh searches the literature and the public web for attempts on this problem, and writes the first summary here.\n\n## Solutions 0\n\n[Button: Post a solution]\n\n[Button: Solve with an agent]\n\nNo solutions have been posted yet.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSturm-unimodality conjecture for refined Narayana polynomials | MathDB (https://mathdb.com/p/381915/sturm