$X-cyclic matroids on $E$E should have a unique maximal element if and only if $\\operatorname{val}_{\\mathcal X}$val X​ is submodular. The forward implication is supplied by the preceding lemma; the converse is the conjectural part, while the more general cyclic formulation is also proposed.\n\n## Progress summary\n\nRefresh\n\nNothing recorded yet. Refresh searches the literature and the public web for attempts on this problem, and writes the first summary here.\n\nSources & references View supporting material\n\n## Primary source\n\nBill Jackson and Shin-ichi Tanigawa, “Maximal Matroids in Weak Order Posets”, arXiv:2102.09901 (2021).\n\nmatroid-theoryposetssubmodularity\n\n0\n\n1 week ago\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCofactor matroid maximality and the valuation rank formula | MathDB (https://mathdb.com/p/349810/cofactor-matroid-maximality-and-the-valuation-rank-formula)\nciteturn2search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; For all $d\\geq1$d≥1, the cofactor matroid $\\mathcal C^{d-2}_{d-1}(K_n)$C d−1 d−2​(K n​) is the unique maximal $K_{d+2}$K d+2​-matroid on $K_n$K n​, and $\\operatorname{val}_{K_{d+2}}$val K d+2​​ is its rank function. ... Bill Jackson and Shin-ichi Tanigawa, “Maximal Matroids in Weak Order Posets”, arXiv:2102.09901 (2021). ... Refresh searches the literature and the public web for attempts on this problem, and writes the first summary here.\n\n# Cofactor matroid maximality and the valuation rank formula\n\nAbout 5 years old · traced to 2021\n\nFor $n$n vertices, let $K_n$K n​ be the complete graph, let $\\mathcal C^{d-2}_{d-1}(K_n)$C d−1 d−2​(K n​) be the cofactor matroid, and let $\\operatorname{val}_{K_{d+2}}$val K d+2​​ be the valuation associated with $K_{d+2}$K d+2​-sequences. Cofactor matroid conjecture. For all $d\\geq1$d≥1, the cofactor matroid $\\mathcal C^{d-2}_{d-1}(K_n)$C d−1 d−2​(K n​) is the unique maximal $K_{d+2}$K d+2​-matroid on $K_n$K n​, and $\\operatorname{val}_{K_{d+2}}$val K d+2​​ is its rank function. The case $d=3$d=3 was recently verified in the cited joint work; the assertion for all $d$d is open.\n\nReferences\n\n  1. Bill Jackson and Shin-ichi Tanigawa, “Maximal Matroids in Weak Order Posets”, arXiv:2102.09901 (2021).\n\ncofactor-matroidsmatroid-theoryrigidity-theory\n\n## Progress summary\n\nRefresh Never refreshed\n\nNothing recorded yet. Refresh searches the literature and the public web for attempts on this problem, and writes the first summary here.\n\n## Solutions 0\n\nNo solutions have been posted yet.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nANDR´ES R. VINDAS MEL´ENDEZ (https://math.hmc.edu/arvm/wp-content/uploads/sites/22/2024/10/ARVM__CV.pdf)\nciteturn2search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.0 years ago; Mel´endez, and Yan Zhuang, A combinatorial proof of a tantalizing symmetry on Catalan objects, sub-\nmitted (arXiv:2212.10586).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDISCRETE ANALYSIS, 2022:3, 32 pp. (https://qmro.qmul.ac.uk/xmlui/bitstream/handle/123456789/78421/Jackson%20Abstract%203-Rigidity%202022%20Published.pdf?sequence=2)\nciteturn2search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; Matroid erection and duality. ... Classiﬁcation of mobile molecules by category theory. ... Combinatorial conditions for the unique completability of ... Maximal matroids in weak order posets. ... //arxiv.org/abs/2102.09901.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nANDR´ES R. VINDAS MEL´ENDEZ (https://math.hmc.edu/arvm/wp-content/uploads/sites/22/2025/01/ARVM__CV.pdf)\nciteturn2search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.8 years ago; Mel´endez, and Yan Zhuang, A combinatorial proof of a tantalizing symmetry on Catalan objects,\nsubmitted (arXiv:2212.10586). ... 2, Paper No.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUC Davis\nUC Davis Electronic Theses and Disserta